# The build context is COPYed wholesale into the image, so anything here would end up in a
# layer — readable by anyone who can pull the image or run `docker history`.

# Secrets. The launch guide has the operator write .env before the first build, so without
# this line SESSION_SECRET, CREDENTIALS_KEY, INTERNAL_API_SECRET and the database password
# are baked into the image (infra/RUNBOOK.md promises the opposite).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Host-built artefacts. node_modules is the dangerous one: a build from a working checkout
# would layer the host's glibc sharp/argon2 binaries over the musl install and fail at
# runtime in ways that look like application bugs.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo
.data
**/.data
test-results
**/test-results

# History and local noise.
.git
.gitignore
*.log
*.zip
coverage
**/coverage
